{
  "_doc": [
    "Maria's Christmas Box plugin for SpectraLab",
    "",
    "Extracts and patches graphics from Maria's Christmas Box 48K .sna snapshot.",
    "",
    "Memory layout at 0xA000 (crosses bank 2 into bank 0):",
    "  +0     : 0x05 (screen count)",
    "  +1..+7 : 'MARIA  ' (name, 7 bytes)",
    "  +8..+11: 4 unknown bytes",
    "  +12..+21: 5 x 16-bit LE offsets (relative to 0xA000)",
    "  +22... : compressed screen data (5 consecutive blocks)",
    "",
    "  Packed data spans from 0xA016 (original RLE) / 0xA016 (with RCS+ZX0),",
    "  crossing from bank 2 (0x8000-0xBFFF) into bank 0 (0xC000-0xFFFF).",
    "  With ZX0: depacker is placed at end of memory ($FE90 = $FF00 - 112),",
    "  keeping the data block (header + compressed screens) portable/sideloadable.",
    "",
    "RLE format (original): 0x00 or 0xFF followed by repeat count byte;",
    "                       all other bytes are literals.",
    "ZX0 format (new): uses SL.ZX0 via the SpectraLab plugin API.",
    "RCS (Reverse Character Scan) reordering applied before ZX0 for better compression.",
    "Each screen decompresses to 6912 bytes (standard SCR).",
    "",
    "Also extracts the loading screen at 0x4000 (uncompressed).",
    "",
    "On extract:",
    "  - Tries ZX0 decompress first (if SL.ZX0 available); validates output is 6912 bytes",
    "  - Falls back to RLE decompress if ZX0 fails or is unavailable",
    "",
    "On save-back (with ZX0):",
    "  - Patches the depacker caller at 0x9602: CALL $FE90 / RET (replaces inline RLE loop)",
    "  - Writes 112-byte smart RCS+ZX0 depacker (dzx0_smartRCS) at $FE90 (end of memory)",
    "  - Reorders bitmap data with RCS for better compression, then compresses with ZX0",
    "  - The smart depacker decompresses and reverses RCS directly to screen (no temp buffer)",
    "  - Places compressed RCS+ZX0 data at 0xA016 (right after header), recalculates offset table",
    "  - Data block (header + packed screens) is portable — can be sideloaded into other programs",
    "  - Packed data must not reach $FE90 (depacker area); overflow check enforces this",
    "  - Falls back to RLE (no patching, no RCS) if SL.ZX0 is unavailable",
    "  - Writes loading screen back to 0x4000",
    "",
    "ZX0 compressor and RCS reordering by Einar Saukas.",
    "dzx0_smartRCS depacker by Einar Saukas.",
    "https://github.com/einar-saukas/ZX0",
    "https://github.com/einar-saukas/RCS",
    "",
    "Z80 code patching detail:",
    "  Original show_image at 0x95EF clears screen, then at 0x95FC:",
    "    95FC: LD DE,$4000    ; destination = screen",
    "    95FF: PUSH IX        ; IX = source (packed data address)",
    "    9601: POP HL         ; HL = source",
    "    9602: <RLE loop>     ; 0x9602-0x9618 = 23 bytes of inline RLE depacker",
    "    9618: RET",
    "  Patched to:",
    "    9602: CALL $FE90     ; call smart RCS+ZX0 depacker at end of memory (HL=src, DE=$4000)",
    "    9605: RET",
    "    9606-9618: 00        ; zeroed out (old RLE code)",
    "",
    "Memory limit:",
    "  - RLE mode: packed data must not extend past 0xFEFF ($FF00-$FFFF = stack/system)",
    "  - ZX0 mode: packed data must not reach $FE90 (112-byte depacker at $FE90-$FEFF)",
    "Save-back will throw an error if packed data overflows the applicable limit.",
    "",
    "IMPORTANT: works directly with fileBytes (offset 27 = address 0x4000)",
    "rather than individual snapshot banks, because packed data crosses",
    "the bank 2 / bank 0 boundary at 0xC000."
  ],

  "id": "maria_48k",
  "name": "Maria's Christmas Box (48K .sna)",
  "version": 4,
  "description": "Extract/patch loading screen + 5 compressed screens (ZX0/RLE) from Maria's Christmas Box 48K snapshot",
  "fileExtensions": [".sna"],
  "type": "js",
  "session": true,

  "jsSource": [
    "// =================================================================",
    "// RLE codec: 0x00/0xFF + count byte; all else literal",
    "// =================================================================",
    "",
    "function rleDecompress(data, offset, length) {",
    "  var out = new Uint8Array(6912);",
    "  var src = offset;",
    "  var end = Math.min(offset + length, data.length);",
    "  var dst = 0;",
    "  while (src < end && dst < 6912) {",
    "    var b = data[src++];",
    "    if (b === 0x00 || b === 0xFF) {",
    "      if (src >= end) break;",
    "      var count = data[src++];",
    "      var stop = Math.min(dst + count, 6912);",
    "      while (dst < stop) out[dst++] = b;",
    "    } else {",
    "      out[dst++] = b;",
    "    }",
    "  }",
    "  return out;",
    "}",
    "",
    "function rleCompress(data) {",
    "  var buf = [];",
    "  var pos = 0;",
    "  while (pos < data.length) {",
    "    var b = data[pos];",
    "    if (b === 0x00 || b === 0xFF) {",
    "      var count = 0;",
    "      while (pos < data.length && data[pos] === b && count < 255) {",
    "        count++; pos++;",
    "      }",
    "      buf.push(b, count);",
    "    } else {",
    "      buf.push(b);",
    "      pos++;",
    "    }",
    "  }",
    "  return new Uint8Array(buf);",
    "}",
    "",
    "// =================================================================",
    "// Decompress a screen block: try ZX0 first, fall back to RLE",
    "// =================================================================",
    "",
    "function decompressScreen(data, offset, length) {",
    "  var block = data.subarray(offset, offset + length);",
    "  if (SL.ZX0) {",
    "    try {",
    "      var result = SL.ZX0.decompress(block);",
    "      if (result && result.length === 6912) return result;",
    "    } catch (e) { /* not ZX0, fall through to RLE */ }",
    "  }",
    "  return rleDecompress(data, offset, length);",
    "}",
    "",
    "// =================================================================",
    "// Compress a screen: RCS reorder + ZX0 if available, otherwise RLE",
    "// RCS (Reverse Character Scan) by Einar Saukas — reorders bitmap",
    "// bytes for better compression. The smart depacker reverses this",
    "// on-the-fly when decompressing to screen memory.",
    "// =================================================================",
    "",
    "function compressScreen(data, zx0) {",
    "  if (zx0 && SL.ZX0) {",
    "    var rcsData = reorderScrToRcs(data);",
    "    return SL.ZX0.compress(rcsData).data;",
    "  }",
    "  return rleCompress(data);",
    "}",
    "",
    "// Reorder SCR bitmap to RCS layout (attrs unchanged)",
    "// SCR address: 010RRppp rrrccccc -> RCS address: 010RRccc ccrrrppp",
    "function reorderScrToRcs(scrBytes) {",
    "  var out = new Uint8Array(6912);",
    "  // Reorder 6144 bitmap bytes",
    "  for (var sector = 0; sector < 3; sector++) {",
    "    for (var col = 0; col < 32; col++) {",
    "      for (var row = 0; row < 8; row++) {",
    "        for (var line = 0; line < 8; line++) {",
    "          var scrAddr = (sector << 11) | (line << 8) | (row << 5) | col;",
    "          var rcsAddr = (sector << 11) | (col << 6) | (row << 3) | line;",
    "          out[rcsAddr] = scrBytes[scrAddr];",
    "        }",
    "      }",
    "    }",
    "  }",
    "  // Copy 768 attribute bytes unchanged",
    "  for (var i = 6144; i < 6912; i++) {",
    "    out[i] = scrBytes[i];",
    "  }",
    "  return out;",
    "}",
    "",
    "// =================================================================",
    "// Smart RCS+ZX0 depacker — 112 bytes, assembled for ORG $FE90",
    "// dzx0_smartRCS by Einar Saukas — decompresses ZX0 data and",
    "// reverses RCS reordering on-the-fly when writing to screen memory.",
    "// When DE < $5800 (bitmap area): converts RCS→SCR address layout.",
    "// When DE >= $5800 (attrs): copies unchanged.",
    "// Parameters: HL = source (compressed), DE = destination ($4000)",
    "// https://github.com/einar-saukas/RCS",
    "// =================================================================",
    "",
    "var DZX0_DEPACKER = [",
    "  // FE90: ld bc,$ffff / push bc / inc bc / ld a,$80",
    "  0x01, 0xFF, 0xFF, 0xC5, 0x03, 0x3E, 0x80,",
    "  // FE97: dzx0r_literals: call dzx0r_elias(FED5)",
    "  0xCD, 0xD5, 0xFE,",
    "  // FE9A: dzx0r_literals_loop: call dzx0r_copy_byte(FEE4)",
    "  0xCD, 0xE4, 0xFE,",
    "  // FE9D: jp pe,dzx0r_literals_loop(FE9A)",
    "  0xEA, 0x9A, 0xFE,",
    "  // FEA0: add a,a / jr c,dzx0r_new_offset(FEBC)",
    "  0x87, 0x38, 0x19,",
    "  // FEA3: call dzx0r_elias(FED5)",
    "  0xCD, 0xD5, 0xFE,",
    "  // FEA6: dzx0r_copy: ex (sp),hl / push hl / add hl,de",
    "  0xE3, 0xE5, 0x19,",
    "  // FEA9: dzx0r_copy_loop: push hl / ex de,hl",
    "  0xE5, 0xEB,",
    "  // FEAB: call dzx0r_convert(FEED) / ex de,hl",
    "  0xCD, 0xED, 0xFE, 0xEB,",
    "  // FEAF: call dzx0r_copy_byte(FEE4)",
    "  0xCD, 0xE4, 0xFE,",
    "  // FEB2: pop hl / inc hl / jp pe,dzx0r_copy_loop(FEA9)",
    "  0xE1, 0x23, 0xEA, 0xA9, 0xFE,",
    "  // FEB7: pop hl / ex (sp),hl / add a,a / jr nc,dzx0r_literals(FE97)",
    "  0xE1, 0xE3, 0x87, 0x30, 0xDB,",
    "  // FEBC: dzx0r_new_offset: pop bc / ld c,$fe",
    "  0xC1, 0x0E, 0xFE,",
    "  // FEBF: call dzx0r_elias_loop(FED6)",
    "  0xCD, 0xD6, 0xFE,",
    "  // FEC2: inc c / ret z / ld b,c / ld c,(hl) / inc hl",
    "  0x0C, 0xC8, 0x41, 0x4E, 0x23,",
    "  // FEC7: rr b / rr c / push bc / ld bc,1",
    "  0xCB, 0x18, 0xCB, 0x19, 0xC5, 0x01, 0x01, 0x00,",
    "  // FECF: call nc,dzx0r_elias_backtrack(FEDD) / inc bc",
    "  0xD4, 0xDD, 0xFE, 0x03,",
    "  // FED3: jr dzx0r_copy(FEA6)",
    "  0x18, 0xD1,",
    "  // FED5: dzx0r_elias: inc c",
    "  0x0C,",
    "  // FED6: dzx0r_elias_loop: add a,a / jr nz,dzx0r_elias_skip(FEDC)",
    "  0x87, 0x20, 0x03,",
    "  // FED9: ld a,(hl) / inc hl / rla",
    "  0x7E, 0x23, 0x17,",
    "  // FEDC: dzx0r_elias_skip: ret c",
    "  0xD8,",
    "  // FEDD: dzx0r_elias_backtrack: add a,a / rl c / rl b",
    "  0x87, 0xCB, 0x11, 0xCB, 0x10,",
    "  // FEE2: jr dzx0r_elias_loop(FED6)",
    "  0x18, 0xF2,",
    "  // FEE4: dzx0r_copy_byte: push de / call dzx0r_convert(FEED)",
    "  0xD5, 0xCD, 0xED, 0xFE,",
    "  // FEE8: ldi / pop de / inc de / ret",
    "  0xED, 0xA0, 0xD1, 0x13, 0xC9,",
    "  // FEED: dzx0r_convert: ex af,af' / ld a,d / cp $58",
    "  0x08, 0x7A, 0xFE, 0x58,",
    "  // FEF1: jr nc,dzx0r_skip(FEFE)",
    "  0x30, 0x0B,",
    "  // FEF3: xor e / and $f8 / xor e / push af",
    "  0xAB, 0xE6, 0xF8, 0xAB, 0xF5,",
    "  // FEF8: xor d / xor e / rlca / rlca / pop de / ld e,a",
    "  0xAA, 0xAB, 0x07, 0x07, 0xD1, 0x5F,",
    "  // FEFE: dzx0r_skip: ex af,af' / ret",
    "  0x08, 0xC9",
    "  // FF00: end — 112 bytes total",
    "];",
    "",
    "var DZX0_SIZE = 112;",
    "var DZX0_BASE_ORG = 0xFE90;  // ORG used when assembling DZX0_DEPACKER",
    "",
    "// Byte offsets of absolute address operands (little-endian) within DZX0_DEPACKER.",
    "// These are the 16-bit address fields of CALL/JP instructions (internal labels).",
    "var DZX0_ABS_OFFSETS = [8, 11, 14, 20, 28, 32, 37, 48, 64, 86];",
    "",
    "// Reassemble depacker for a different ORG address",
    "function reassembleDepacker(newOrg) {",
    "  var delta = newOrg - DZX0_BASE_ORG;",
    "  var out = new Uint8Array(DZX0_DEPACKER);",
    "  for (var i = 0; i < DZX0_ABS_OFFSETS.length; i++) {",
    "    var off = DZX0_ABS_OFFSETS[i];",
    "    var addr = out[off] | (out[off + 1] << 8);",
    "    addr += delta;",
    "    out[off] = addr & 0xFF;",
    "    out[off + 1] = (addr >> 8) & 0xFF;",
    "  }",
    "  return out;",
    "}",
    "",
    "// =================================================================",
    "// Constants",
    "// =================================================================",
    "",
    "var SNA_HEADER   = 27;",
    "var DATA_ADDR    = 0xA000;",
    "var MEM_BASE     = 0x4000;   // First byte after SNA header",
    "var HEADER_SIZE  = 22;       // 1+7+4+10 bytes before packed data",
    "var OFFSET_TBL   = 12;      // Offset table at +12 (5 x 16-bit LE)",
    "var SCREEN_COUNT = 5;",
    "var SCR_SIZE     = 6912;",
    "var MAX_ADDR     = 0xFF00;  // 0xFF00-0xFFFF reserved (stack/system)",
    "var GAME_NAME    = 'MARIA';  // max 7 chars, padded with trailing spaces",
    "var NAME_OFFSET  = 1;       // name starts at +1 from DATA_ADDR",
    "var NAME_LENGTH  = 7;",
    "",
    "// Depacker caller patch addresses",
    "var UNPACK_CALL  = 0x9602;  // Start of inline RLE loop in show_image",
    "var UNPACK_END   = 0x9618;  // Last byte (RET) of inline RLE loop",
    "",
    "// Convert Z80 address to file offset",
    "function addr2off(addr) {",
    "  return SNA_HEADER + (addr - MEM_BASE);",
    "}",
    "",
    "// =================================================================",
    "// Plugin",
    "// =================================================================",
    "",
    "plugin = {",
    "",
    "  extract: function(fileBytes) {",
    "    var pics = [];",
    "    var base = addr2off(DATA_ADDR);  // file offset of 0xA000",
    "",
    "    // 1) Loading screen at 0x4000 (uncompressed)",
    "    var loadScr = fileBytes.subarray(SNA_HEADER, SNA_HEADER + SCR_SIZE);",
    "    pics.push({",
    "      name:   'Loading Screen',",
    "      format: 'scr',",
    "      data:   loadScr",
    "    });",
    "",
    "    // 2) Read 5 x 16-bit LE offsets from the header",
    "    var offsets = [];",
    "    for (var i = 0; i < SCREEN_COUNT; i++) {",
    "      var pos = base + OFFSET_TBL + i * 2;",
    "      offsets.push(fileBytes[pos] | (fileBytes[pos + 1] << 8));",
    "    }",
    "",
    "    // 3) Decompress each packed screen (auto-detects ZX0 vs RLE)",
    "    for (var i = 0; i < SCREEN_COUNT; i++) {",
    "      var packStart = base + offsets[i];",
    "      var packLen;",
    "      if (i < SCREEN_COUNT - 1) {",
    "        packLen = offsets[i + 1] - offsets[i];",
    "      } else {",
    "        packLen = fileBytes.length - packStart;",
    "      }",
    "      var scr = decompressScreen(fileBytes, packStart, packLen);",
    "      pics.push({",
    "        name:   'Screen ' + (i + 1),",
    "        format: 'scr',",
    "        data:   scr",
    "      });",
    "    }",
    "",
    "    return pics;",
    "  },",
    "",
    "  patch: function(originalBytes, pictures) {",
    "    var useZX0 = SL.ZX0 && confirm('Use ZX0 compression (smaller size)?\\n\\nCancel = keep original RLE compression');",
    "    var method = useZX0 ? 'ZX0' : 'RLE';",
    "",
    "    // 4) Create progress overlay immediately after user chooses",
    "    var overlay = document.createElement('div');",
    "    overlay.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;background:rgba(0,0,0,0.5);z-index:999999;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center';",
    "    var box = document.createElement('div');",
    "    box.style.cssText = 'background:#222;color:#eee;padding:20px 30px;border-radius:8px;min-width:320px;font-family:sans-serif;font-size:14px';",
    "    var title = document.createElement('div');",
    "    title.style.cssText = 'margin-bottom:12px;font-size:16px;font-weight:bold';",
    "    title.textContent = 'Compressing (' + method + ')...';",
    "    var barOuter = document.createElement('div');",
    "    barOuter.style.cssText = 'background:#444;height:20px;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:10px';",
    "    var barInner = document.createElement('div');",
    "    barInner.style.cssText = 'background:#4caf50;height:100%;width:0%;transition:width 0.2s';",
    "    barOuter.appendChild(barInner);",
    "    var info = document.createElement('div');",
    "    info.style.cssText = 'font-size:13px;color:#aaa;white-space:pre';",
    "    info.textContent = '';",
    "    var btnRow = document.createElement('div');",
    "    btnRow.style.cssText = 'margin-top:14px;text-align:right';",
    "    var btn = document.createElement('button');",
    "    btn.style.cssText = 'padding:6px 20px;font-size:14px;cursor:pointer;border:none;border-radius:4px;background:#666;color:#eee';",
    "    btn.textContent = 'Cancel';",
    "    var cancelled = false;",
    "    btn.onclick = function() { cancelled = true; };",
    "    btnRow.appendChild(btn);",
    "    box.appendChild(title);",
    "    box.appendChild(barOuter);",
    "    box.appendChild(info);",
    "    box.appendChild(btnRow);",
    "    overlay.appendChild(box);",
    "    document.body.appendChild(overlay);",
    "",
    "    var base = addr2off(DATA_ADDR);",
    "    var packed = [];",
    "    var report = '';",
    "",
    "    function delay() {",
    "      return new Promise(function(resolve) { setTimeout(resolve, 0); });",
    "    }",
    "",
    "    // Yield to let browser paint the overlay, then do setup + compression",
    "    return delay().then(function() {",
    "      // 1) Write loading screen back at 0x4000",
    "      if (pictures.length > 0 && pictures[0].data.length >= SCR_SIZE) {",
    "        originalBytes.set(",
    "          pictures[0].data.subarray(0, SCR_SIZE),",
    "          SNA_HEADER",
    "        );",
    "      }",
    "",
    "      // 2) Write game name at +1 from header (7 bytes, space-padded)",
    "      var name = (GAME_NAME + '       ').substring(0, NAME_LENGTH);",
    "      for (var c = 0; c < NAME_LENGTH; c++) {",
    "        originalBytes[base + NAME_OFFSET + c] = name.charCodeAt(c);",
    "      }",
    "",
    "      // 3) If using ZX0: patch the depacker caller and inject RCS+ZX0 depacker",
    "      var dataStart = HEADER_SIZE;  // 22 — data right after header (same for both modes)",
    "      if (useZX0) {",
    "        // 3a) Place depacker at end of memory: DEPACKER_ADDR = MAX_ADDR - DZX0_SIZE",
    "        var depackerAddr = MAX_ADDR - DZX0_SIZE;  // $FF00 - 112 = $FE90",
    "",
    "        // 3b) Patch caller at 0x9602: CALL depackerAddr / RET / zero out rest",
    "        var callOff = addr2off(UNPACK_CALL);",
    "        originalBytes[callOff]     = 0xCD;  // CALL",
    "        originalBytes[callOff + 1] = depackerAddr & 0xFF;",
    "        originalBytes[callOff + 2] = (depackerAddr >> 8) & 0xFF;",
    "        originalBytes[callOff + 3] = 0xC9;  // RET",
    "        // Zero out remaining old RLE code (0x9606-0x9618)",
    "        var endOff = addr2off(UNPACK_END);",
    "        for (var z = callOff + 4; z <= endOff; z++) {",
    "          originalBytes[z] = 0x00;",
    "        }",
    "",
    "        // 3c) Reassemble depacker for the actual ORG address",
    "        var depacker = reassembleDepacker(depackerAddr);",
    "",
    "        // 3d) Write depacker at end of memory",
    "        var depackerOff = addr2off(depackerAddr);",
    "        for (var d = 0; d < DZX0_SIZE; d++) {",
    "          originalBytes[depackerOff + d] = depacker[d];",
    "        }",
    "      }",
    "      return dataStart;",
    "    }).then(function(dataStart) {",
    "      // 5) Compress screens with progress updates",
    "      function compressStep(i) {",
    "        if (cancelled) return Promise.reject(new Error('Cancelled'));",
    "        if (i >= SCREEN_COUNT) return Promise.resolve();",
    "        var picIdx = i + 1;",
    "        if (picIdx < pictures.length && pictures[picIdx].data.length > 0) {",
    "          packed.push(compressScreen(pictures[picIdx].data, useZX0));",
    "        } else {",
    "          packed.push(new Uint8Array(0));",
    "        }",
    "        report += 'Screen ' + (i + 1) + ': ' + packed[i].length + ' bytes\\n';",
    "        var pct = Math.round(((i + 1) / SCREEN_COUNT) * 100);",
    "        barInner.style.width = pct + '%';",
    "        info.textContent = report;",
    "        title.textContent = 'Compressing (' + method + ')... ' + (i + 1) + '/' + SCREEN_COUNT;",
    "        return delay().then(function() { return compressStep(i + 1); });",
    "      }",
    "",
    "      return compressStep(0).then(function() {",
    "        // 6) Calculate new offsets and write offset table",
    "        var offsets = [dataStart];",
    "        for (var i = 0; i < SCREEN_COUNT - 1; i++) {",
    "          offsets.push(offsets[i] + packed[i].length);",
    "        }",
    "        for (var i = 0; i < SCREEN_COUNT; i++) {",
    "          var pos = base + OFFSET_TBL + i * 2;",
    "          originalBytes[pos]     = offsets[i] & 0xFF;",
    "          originalBytes[pos + 1] = (offsets[i] >> 8) & 0xFF;",
    "        }",
    "",
    "        // 7) Check for memory overflow",
    "        // When ZX0: depacker lives at MAX_ADDR - DZX0_SIZE, data must not reach it",
    "        var dataLimit = useZX0 ? (MAX_ADDR - DZX0_SIZE) : MAX_ADDR;",
    "        var maxFileOff = addr2off(dataLimit);",
    "        var totalPacked = 0;",
    "        for (var i = 0; i < SCREEN_COUNT; i++) totalPacked += packed[i].length;",
    "        var endPos = base + dataStart + totalPacked;",
    "        if (endPos > maxFileOff) {",
    "          throw new Error(",
    "            'Packed data too large! Overflow by ' + (endPos - maxFileOff) + ' bytes.\\n\\n' + report",
    "          );",
    "        }",
    "",
    "        // 8) Write packed data consecutively",
    "        var writePos = base + dataStart;",
    "        for (var i = 0; i < SCREEN_COUNT; i++) {",
    "          originalBytes.set(packed[i], writePos);",
    "          writePos += packed[i].length;",
    "        }",
    "",
    "        // 9) Zero out leftover space up to data limit (not into depacker area)",
    "        var clearEnd = Math.min(maxFileOff, writePos + 8192);",
    "        for (var i = writePos; i < clearEnd; i++) {",
    "          originalBytes[i] = 0;",
    "        }",
    "",
    "        // Show free memory, wait for user to close",
    "        var freeBytes = maxFileOff - endPos;",
    "        report += '\\nFree: ' + freeBytes + ' bytes';",
    "        info.textContent = report;",
    "        title.textContent = 'Done (' + method + ')';",
    "        barInner.style.width = '100%';",
    "",
    "        return new Promise(function(resolve) {",
    "          btn.textContent = 'Close';",
    "          btn.style.background = '#4caf50';",
    "          btn.onclick = function() { resolve(); };",
    "        });",
    "      }).then(function() {",
    "        document.body.removeChild(overlay);",
    "        return originalBytes;",
    "      });",
    "    }).catch(function(err) {",
    "      document.body.removeChild(overlay);",
    "      if (err.message === 'Cancelled') return null;",
    "      throw err;",
    "    });",
    "  }",
    "",
    "};"
  ]
}
